From 25d33fcb0724b397b996cf095b79e65fdefabde4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artemonim <Artemonim@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:18:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/23] feat(agent): opt-in TTFT service-tier escalation for
 OpenRouter

Second commit of the #100711 service-tier split (may be dropped independently
if tiers without the control loop are preferred).

agent.service_tier_escalation (default off): streaming time-to-first-token
ladder flex -> default -> priority. consecutive_slow_requests slow successful
streams climb one rung for the rest of the turn; the next user prompt resets
to the configured base tier. Applied as the last step of
effective_request_overrides without mutating canonical agent.service_tier /
request_overrides; a wire-tier snapshot keeps outer retries of the same
logical request on the attempt's original tier. Fallback/restore rebases the
ladder onto the new model's base tier (rungs carry over); switch_model resets.

Hard-gated off for cron, batch, subagents, background tasks and pinned
sessions. Default-off path is hook-free on the streaming hot path. Codex and
non-streaming requests produce no observation (documented).

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
